{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 66,
    "dDurationMs": 534,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We all know that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600,
    "dDurationMs": 5700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Japan has the highest government debt\nin the world, at 226% of GDP"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6600,
    "dDurationMs": 2866,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in 2023."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9466,
    "dDurationMs": 4334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That that is almost double that of France\nor the UK."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14000,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Two countries that have faced repeated\ndebt crisis, where investors are rapidly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18900,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "demanded higher interest rates\nin response to government spending plans."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24133,
    "dDurationMs": 3733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yet, while Japan's economy\nhas stagnated much more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27866,
    "dDurationMs": 3934,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than these others do,\nand the population is aging much faster."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31833,
    "dDurationMs": 4433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Investors seem willing to keep lending\nJapan a lot of money"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36266,
    "dDurationMs": 3334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at much lower interest rates\nthan other countries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39933,
    "dDurationMs": 2033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what the heck is going on?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41966,
    "dDurationMs": 4967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, according to a recent paper\nby economists Tim Dou and Lustig,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46933,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the answer may be surprisingly simple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50133,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Actually, everyone has just been looking\nat the wrong number."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53466,
    "dDurationMs": 5434,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, Japan's total official government\ndebt is well over 220% of GDP,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59233,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but that number leaves out\nsomething important."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61933,
    "dDurationMs": 4667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unlike most Western governments, Japan's\nconsolidated government,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66600,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which includes institutions\nlike the central Bank and public pension"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70500,
    "dDurationMs": 4666,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "funds, holds a massive financial\nportfolio of stocks and bonds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75300,
    "dDurationMs": 6300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that was worth about 192% of GDP\nin 2020 fourth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81966,
    "dDurationMs": 3967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, total debt of the entire\nJapanese government and public pension"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85933,
    "dDurationMs": 6433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "funds and central banks was also higher\nthan the official number at 270% of GDP."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92700,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But netting those two out means\nthat Japan's true"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96500,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "government debt suddenly looks far\nless alarming."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100200,
    "dDurationMs": 3866,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Closer to 77% of GDP."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104166,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we look at similar calculations\nfor the US and United Kingdom,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108566,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then it becomes clear that actually,\nwhile Japan"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111566,
    "dDurationMs": 3534,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has way, way more total debt,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115566,
    "dDurationMs": 4734,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if we look at net debt\ncalculated by debt minus financial assets,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120566,
    "dDurationMs": 5367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Japan's debt is actually the lowest\nof these three countries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126166,
    "dDurationMs": 3667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because Western governments\nlike those in the US and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130066,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "especially in the UK,\nhave far fewer assets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134800,
    "dDurationMs": 2233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we have just been looking\nat the wrong number."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137033,
    "dDurationMs": 1367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, it's really that simple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138400,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is all we need to answer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139800,
    "dDurationMs": 4033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Our main question why Japan's debt\ndynamics make no sense at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144133,
    "dDurationMs": 2167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Japan's government\npays a lower interest rate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146300,
    "dDurationMs": 3933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and does not have massive inflation\nproblems simply because,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150233,
    "dDurationMs": 3833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rather than just spending on the elderly,\nthe Japanese state"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154066,
    "dDurationMs": 5900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has been buying a lot of financial assets\nand especially foreign assets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160233,
    "dDurationMs": 4267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this all happened at the same time\nthat it was accumulating a massive debt."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164866,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Having sky high debt and assets\ncan also explain some other things"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168766,
    "dDurationMs": 4067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that I've been puzzling over, like why,\ndespite having a smaller and smaller"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173066,
    "dDurationMs": 1834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "international economy, Japan"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174900,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "keeps showing up as one of the biggest\nowners of foreign assets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178966,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like here in this graph, which shows that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182166,
    "dDurationMs": 3634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's not Saudi Arabia, not even China."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185833,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, it's Japan that is by far\nthe largest holder of U.S."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189533,
    "dDurationMs": 667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "debt."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190200,
    "dDurationMs": 5233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why I, chin, do and Lustig refer\nto the Japanese government in their paper"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195700,
    "dDurationMs": 3466,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as a giant sovereign wealth fund."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199333,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But interestingly,\nrather than funding that giant wealth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202233,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fund with oil, money like Norway\nand the Gulf states have done,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205300,
    "dDurationMs": 4866,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Japan's government funded it with money\nborrowed from the Japanese people."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210300,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So for that reason, I would actually argue\nthat Japan's government"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214533,
    "dDurationMs": 3767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "complex has become like a dairy trading"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218800,
    "dDurationMs": 2933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "giant, hedge fund borrowing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 221733,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from people in yen that low interest rates"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226066,
    "dDurationMs": 3734,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and lending it out to the world,\ninvesting in the world"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229800,
    "dDurationMs": 4233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in dollars at a very high interest rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 234333,
    "dDurationMs": 1533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But hey, wait a minute."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235866,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Doesn't that sound kind of risky?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238366,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why is Japan's government\nborrowing so much money"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242266,
    "dDurationMs": 3734,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to then\ninvest a lot of that in foreign assets?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246066,
    "dDurationMs": 4434,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Is that sustainable,\nor is it a giant bubble waiting to burst?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250600,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To answer these questions,\nwe need to understand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253866,
    "dDurationMs": 3234,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how Japan's government\nbecame a giant hedge fund."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257266,
    "dDurationMs": 5767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You see, unlike the Western government,\nsmall state ideal, Japan's government"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263033,
    "dDurationMs": 5167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "apparatus always had both a lot of assets\nand a lot of debt."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268500,
    "dDurationMs": 2833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "During the postwar economic miracle\nwhere Japan was growing at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271333,
    "dDurationMs": 5333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an astonishing rate of 10%, the Japanese\ngovernment complex essentially already"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276666,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "acted like a giant bank via"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279666,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the government owned Japan Post,\na public bank."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283566,
    "dDurationMs": 4267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It essentially borrowed\nfrom the Japanese people by offering them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287833,
    "dDurationMs": 4667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ultra low deposit accounts,\nwhich they took in mass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292500,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because through a law in 1947,\nthe Japanese government had essentially"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296500,
    "dDurationMs": 3533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "outlawed\nhigh interest rates on savings accounts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 300266,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it could borrow\nat very low interest rates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302966,
    "dDurationMs": 3034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And those funds were then\nessentially funneled"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306000,
    "dDurationMs": 6100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the government owned Fiscal Investment\nand Loan Fund, short for filth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312433,
    "dDurationMs": 4133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which then used these\nto rebuild Japan's industries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316566,
    "dDurationMs": 4267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and infrastructure\nat much higher interest rates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321166,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is very different\nthan how we are used to thinking"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 324366,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about government investments in the West\nin three ways."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 327900,
    "dDurationMs": 2566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, it was not the central government\nthat borrowed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330466,
    "dDurationMs": 3967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was the post office\nthat essentially borrowed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334833,
    "dDurationMs": 4667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then second, the Japanese government\ndid not spent money on infrastructure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339500,
    "dDurationMs": 4466,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And no, no, this was the fiscal investment\nand loan fund"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343966,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that invested in infrastructure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345966,
    "dDurationMs": 4167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And third, because it kept interest rates\nlow through the law,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 350333,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Japanese government essentially acted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353633,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as a giant bank,\nborrowing at very low interest rates"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358233,
    "dDurationMs": 3433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then lending them out\nat much higher interest rates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 362133,
    "dDurationMs": 3767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So just to illustrate\nhow raw government debt numbers often hide"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365900,
    "dDurationMs": 1933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the most important details,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 367833,
    "dDurationMs": 3767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "none of this showed up\nin official government debt numbers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 371633,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the time, Japan's\nmassive borrowing from Japan Post"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375700,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was, of course, not part of\nofficial Japanese debt numbers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 379700,
    "dDurationMs": 2533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But also on the other side,\nJapan's massive investments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382233,
    "dDurationMs": 2033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "via the Fiscal Investment Loan Fund."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 384266,
    "dDurationMs": 3734,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Film was not part of government\nspending numbers either."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 388366,
    "dDurationMs": 2834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then, last\nbut not least, while governments publish"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391200,
    "dDurationMs": 3033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "interest service costs\nin statistics offices,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394566,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this interest rate profit\nthat they made was not published anywhere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399800,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However,\nmaybe that was not such a bad thing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402000,
    "dDurationMs": 3566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because seeing the entire story\nof how government debt works"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 406233,
    "dDurationMs": 1333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can be kind of scary."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 407566,
    "dDurationMs": 1634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "People already installed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409200,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "debt clocks, dead records, meaningless\ndebt numbers to scare people."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 413233,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine what would happen if you tell them\nnot just Japan's government,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418033,
    "dDurationMs": 3933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the government of many, many\ndeveloping countries essentially acted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421966,
    "dDurationMs": 4634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like giant public banks\nto grow their economies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427300,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It would be a shame\nif they put a stop to that,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 430000,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because Japan's government bank structure\nworked really well, creating"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434800,
    "dDurationMs": 4833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one of the most impressive growth stories\nof all time that then China repeated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439933,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if acting like a giant bank,\nbetting on your own economy sounds scary,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445033,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "imagine telling the Japanese people today\nthat their government is now acting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 449700,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like a giant hedge fund, using\ntheir borrowed money from Japanese people"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455266,
    "dDurationMs": 4867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not to invest in Japan's economy,\nbut rather betting on US"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 460133,
    "dDurationMs": 4167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "government debt,\nthe US stock market and Chinese factories."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464400,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what happened?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465233,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why did Japan's government"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 466633,
    "dDurationMs": 4167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "turn from a giant bank into a giant, risky\nglobal hedge fund?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 470966,
    "dDurationMs": 1234,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's actually quite simple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472200,
    "dDurationMs": 2633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Japan's economy got up to the west"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474833,
    "dDurationMs": 4067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and its population\nstarted to get old really quickly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478900,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So of course, economic growth\nslowed down by a lot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482233,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in the early 1990s, after a gigantic\nbubble popped, we all know what happened."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488166,
    "dDurationMs": 5567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Japan's economy completely flatlined,\nand therefore investing in the Japanese"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 493733,
    "dDurationMs": 4567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "economy suddenly became far\nless profitable as well, meaning that this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 498300,
    "dDurationMs": 3266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "entire model, acting like a giant bank\nsuddenly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501566,
    "dDurationMs": 3334,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "also became much less profitable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 505400,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But given that interest\nrates also went down by a lot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 510633,
    "dDurationMs": 2267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it still worked somewhat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 512900,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This was not necessarily\nthe end of this model."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 515300,
    "dDurationMs": 3633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, what really ended this government\nBank of Japan model is that after"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 518933,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Japanese economic miracle stopped\nworking, Japan became more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522433,
    "dDurationMs": 4667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and more convinced that Western free\nmarket ideas were the answer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527266,
    "dDurationMs": 3134,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in free market economies\nlike the UK or US,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 530400,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the government does not act like a giant\nbank, the economy's biggest bank."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 535766,
    "dDurationMs": 3734,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in the early 2000, the bill was cut"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 539500,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from these cheap bank deposit funding."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542666,
    "dDurationMs": 2934,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then much later, Japan Post itself"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 545600,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was cut into pieces and privatized."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 549100,
    "dDurationMs": 3666,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The time had come for free market\neconomics in Japan, and therefore"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 552800,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the government had to act much more\nlike a typical Western government,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556533,
    "dDurationMs": 3567,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "simply funding its spending with taxes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 560333,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, unlike Western governments\nat the time, Japan in the early 2000"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 565233,
    "dDurationMs": 5700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was the first country to start facing\na serious, serious demographic crisis,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571200,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this meant that rapidly increasing\npension costs, rapidly increasing health"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 575500,
    "dDurationMs": 3033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "care costs,\ncombined with economic stagnation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 578533,
    "dDurationMs": 3133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meaning less or less\ntax income for the government."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581700,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the logical thing for the Japanese\ngovernment complex to have done"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 586900,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then at that point is to start\nselling many of its pension assets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591733,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then because this was not going\nto be enough to either start spending"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596433,
    "dDurationMs": 5700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "less on other things like education\nor to raise taxes, in other words,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 602400,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "following economic orthodoxy, Japan\nshould have implemented austerity, but"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 608900,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because it already had a stagnant economy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 612300,
    "dDurationMs": 3266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the gains in advice is not to do that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 615600,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead, after having stopped\nbeing a giant national bank, it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 619400,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then became a giant hedge fund."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 622733,
    "dDurationMs": 2767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So rather than selling pension assets,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625500,
    "dDurationMs": 5566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it started borrowing on a massive scale,\nissuing bonds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 631233,
    "dDurationMs": 4167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to cover ever increasing\nsocial security costs for pensioners."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635700,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there was a problem borrowing fire."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 638100,
    "dDurationMs": 3933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The bond market alone\ncould have been quite expensive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642200,
    "dDurationMs": 3766,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, quite conveniently and officially\njust to try to raise inflation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 645966,
    "dDurationMs": 3534,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and get the economy going again,\nthe Bank of Japan, which is of course"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 649500,
    "dDurationMs": 4766,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "part of the Japanese government complex,\nstarted buying bonds from private banks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 654633,
    "dDurationMs": 5333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in exchange for so-called reserves,\nwhich they can create central bank money,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660266,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which quite conveniently pays\nvery low interest rates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 665733,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And therefore, essentially,\njust as in the Japan Post era, Japan"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 669600,
    "dDurationMs": 2666,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "government was again\nborrowing from the Japanese people"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672266,
    "dDurationMs": 1434,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at very low interest rates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 673700,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now, rather than doing it\nvia national banks like Japan Post,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 678200,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it did so indirectly via the central bank."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 682200,
    "dDurationMs": 2166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But crucially, the result was,\nof course, the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684366,
    "dDurationMs": 3734,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Japan's government could again borrow\nat ultra low interest rates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 688400,
    "dDurationMs": 5366,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But okay, now how do we get to the Gary\nTrade hedge fund part of this story?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694000,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, in the early 2000,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 695700,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because Japan's central bank had been\nbuying all the steps, quantitative easing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700100,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Japanese interest rates were much lower\nthan in other major economies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 705300,
    "dDurationMs": 3666,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "such as in US dollar markets\nor euro markets or in China."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 709466,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so, logically,\nmany private Japanese investors"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 713166,
    "dDurationMs": 3234,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "famously started the so-called carry"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716400,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trades,\nborrowing at ultra low rates in yen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 720600,
    "dDurationMs": 3766,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to then invest at higher\ninterest rates in foreign currencies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 724633,
    "dDurationMs": 1267,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what is less well known"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 725900,
    "dDurationMs": 4333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that the Japan government complex\nessentially did the same thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 730233,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as it turns out, this would actually\nsave Japan's government"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 733966,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from a full blown pension crisis\nin three ways."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 738966,
    "dDurationMs": 3834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, it\nreignited the old Japan government complex"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 743200,
    "dDurationMs": 4866,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "profit machine because they were borrowing\nvery cheaply via the central bank."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 748066,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when they're investing\nin foreign securities,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 751133,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which earned a much higher interest rate\nabroad."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 754866,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Second, while asset prices in\nJapan would go up by quite a bit,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 759133,
    "dDurationMs": 4967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "asset prices\nabroad would go up by way more than that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 764433,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And finally, third,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 765633,
    "dDurationMs": 4533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in this time period, the Japanese\nyen would actually fall by a lot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 770166,
    "dDurationMs": 4067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So essentially\ntheir debt would become worth less while"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 774233,
    "dDurationMs": 3067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their foreign assets would again\nbecome worth much more."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 777500,
    "dDurationMs": 3566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And to see how important a falling\nyen would become for the Japan government"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 781066,
    "dDurationMs": 5667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "complex, imagine that a state owned\npension fund would buy 100 worth of U.S."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 786733,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Treasury bonds in 2013,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 789933,
    "dDurationMs": 3233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when the exchange rate\nwas at ¥100 for a dollar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 793200,
    "dDurationMs": 4666,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it paid about ¥10,000 for these bonds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 798066,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, fast forward to 2024,\nwhen the exchange rate is roughly ¥150"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 803866,
    "dDurationMs": 900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "per dollar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804766,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now these bonds that they held were still\nworth 100, let's say in dollar terms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 809933,
    "dDurationMs": 2367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nothing changed\nabout the investment itself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 812300,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now when the pension fund converts\nback to yen,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 816166,
    "dDurationMs": 4767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these same bonds are worth 15 K in yen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 821133,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's a 50% gain\npurely from the exchange rate moving."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 825466,
    "dDurationMs": 3234,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is exactly what happened\nto the entire"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 828966,
    "dDurationMs": 4034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Japanese foreign\nportfolio over the past decade."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 833300,
    "dDurationMs": 4066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this effect has been so big\nthat between 2012 and 2024,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 837533,
    "dDurationMs": 2867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Japan's net debt remember,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840400,
    "dDurationMs": 4433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "assets minus liabilities, debt\nactually went down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 844833,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from 118% of GDP in 2012"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 849666,
    "dDurationMs": 4367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to net debt of 77% of GDP today."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854533,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not because they borrowed less."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 856033,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To the contrary,\nthey bought more, but because foreign"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 859700,
    "dDurationMs": 3566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and to a lesser extent, local asset\nmarkets went up by so much."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 863300,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the yen almost collapsed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 866600,
    "dDurationMs": 4166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So while Japan's net debt\nlooks pretty good on paper,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 870766,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "much better than expected, it's\nnot the case that Japan was secretly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 875066,
    "dDurationMs": 3934,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a fiscally responsible country,\nand that it borrowed simply to invest"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 879233,
    "dDurationMs": 3033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in foreign markets, and that it knew\nthis would go up in value."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 882466,
    "dDurationMs": 3534,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sure, that was a small part of the story,\nbut the biggest part of the story is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 886000,
    "dDurationMs": 3433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "simply that Japan got very, very lucky."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 889800,
    "dDurationMs": 2333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what can go up and go down as well?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 892133,
    "dDurationMs": 4933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So could Japan's so far lucky financial\ngambling soon become a major risk."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 897566,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We'll get to that after word\nfrom our advertising sponsor, Storyblocks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 901966,
    "dDurationMs": 667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You see, one thing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 902633,
    "dDurationMs": 3667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I've learned after five years on YouTube\nis that explainer videos live or die."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 906300,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By their visuals, you can have\nthe sharpest analysis in the world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 909366,
    "dDurationMs": 4534,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you're just staring at a talking\nhead, in this case, people switch off."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 913933,
    "dDurationMs": 3133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You need footage\nthat makes the story come to life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 917400,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The problem is that finding good stock"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 919200,
    "dDurationMs": 3733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "footage used to eat up way more of my time\nthan I'd like to admit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 922966,
    "dDurationMs": 2834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Jumping between platforms,\nworrying about licensing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 925800,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "downloading clips that just end up looking\ncheap."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 928833,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Storyblocks\nsolves all of that in one place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 931966,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a massive library of real,\nprofessionally shot footage"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 936200,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "made by actual filmmakers,\nnot AI generated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 939333,
    "dDurationMs": 2933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And a lot of the clips\nthat you've been watching in this video"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 942266,
    "dDurationMs": 4734,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "showcase in Japan, like these super cool\nstock footage of the 1960s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 947000,
    "dDurationMs": 4133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Japanese factory workers,\nactually came from Storyblocks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 951566,
    "dDurationMs": 3834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Personally, the most valuable service\nfor me is the licensing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 955633,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Everything is royalty free and free\ncleared for monetized YouTube videos,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 960533,
    "dDurationMs": 4167,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so I'm never second guessing\nwhether I can actually use something"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 965000,
    "dDurationMs": 2033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that alone saves me hours every week."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 967033,
    "dDurationMs": 3467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hours I can put back into the research\nand storytelling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 970500,
    "dDurationMs": 3533,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that you actually hopefully come to money\na macro for it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 974400,
    "dDurationMs": 3333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So start selling\nbetter stories with the tools that I use."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 977866,
    "dDurationMs": 5700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Head over to storyblocks.com/money macro\nor click the link in the description."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 983600,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They are also offering a limited time\ndiscount for my audience"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 987700,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only through my link in the description."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 990700,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So go click it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 992700,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now first back to Japan,\nthe lucky country."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 996533,
    "dDurationMs": 4133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So far its financial adventures\nhave not only kept debt low,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1000800,
    "dDurationMs": 2933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they significantly reduced it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1003733,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But is that sustainable?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1006333,
    "dDurationMs": 4967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's ask ourselves, how likely is Japan's\ngovernment debt hedge fund to explode?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1011666,
    "dDurationMs": 3634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To answer that question, I think we should\nrevisit the three elements that made"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1015300,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Japan's big hedge fund gamble\nso successful in the first place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1019533,
    "dDurationMs": 433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Vector."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1019966,
    "dDurationMs": 4234,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Number one, foreign interest rates\nare higher than local interest rates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1024666,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Factor number two foreign assets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1026566,
    "dDurationMs": 2434,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Markets continue to go up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1029000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then of course, very very crucial."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1031000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The yen continues to go down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1034266,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Aren't these trends likely to continue."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1037400,
    "dDurationMs": 3633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, given that for the foreseeable\nfuture, Japan is still going"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1041066,
    "dDurationMs": 4834,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be the oldest country by far,\neven compared to its major investment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1045900,
    "dDurationMs": 4233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "destinations like China\nand especially the US."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1050300,
    "dDurationMs": 4133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It looks like the Japan had different\nstrategy does continue to make sense."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1054800,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After all, as Japan continues to age,\nit will likely be able to produce"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1058333,
    "dDurationMs": 1733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "less and consume more."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1060066,
    "dDurationMs": 2667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore, a need to import more."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1062733,
    "dDurationMs": 3433,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the demand for the\nyen will likely to continue"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1066166,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to fall, and the\nyen will likely continue to weaken."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1069200,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are two major risks, though,\nthat Japan needs to watch out for it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1073700,
    "dDurationMs": 3133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first is obvious it's geopolitics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1077066,
    "dDurationMs": 5467,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, if your strategy is to invest\nabroad to sustain your aging population."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1082766,
    "dDurationMs": 3634,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well that's right, the only works\nif foreign countries allow it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1086533,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, if the world completely globalize"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1089833,
    "dDurationMs": 3033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Japan loses its foreign assets"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1093100,
    "dDurationMs": 3466,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "completely, then Japan's debt to GDP"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1096733,
    "dDurationMs": 3867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "suddenly\nin one fell swoop, goes up from 77%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1100800,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to about 140% of GDP."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1104333,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the second more probable risk"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1106533,
    "dDurationMs": 3667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is inflation, as we've seen to mean\nit is net debt."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1110500,
    "dDurationMs": 3166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Japan benefits from an ever weaker yen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1113800,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because it raises their assets\nand make their debt worth less."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1118433,
    "dDurationMs": 3933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, of course, if the yen goes down\nall the time, imports"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1122366,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "become more expensive\nall the time in Japan, causing inflation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1126400,
    "dDurationMs": 1966,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And to make matters even worse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1128366,
    "dDurationMs": 4367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hedge fund Japan works best\nif the central bank"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1132733,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "interest rate\nis much lower than it is abroad."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1136200,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the most common way\ncentral banks control inflation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1139433,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is by raising interest rates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1142466,
    "dDurationMs": 3367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If inflation gets too high,\nbut if it does so by too much, then"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1145833,
    "dDurationMs": 4667,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this entire hedge Fund Japan model\nsuddenly works much less."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1150800,
    "dDurationMs": 5066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So will Japan, famous for deflation, soon\nhave an inflation problem?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1156200,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is the trillion yen question."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1158900,
    "dDurationMs": 4333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And sadly for Japan, famous\nprofessor Charles Goodhart from the London"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1163233,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "School of Economics has predicted\nthat once populations get too old,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1168300,
    "dDurationMs": 3733,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they will likely face\nmore and more inflation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1172266,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as they stop producing\nand saving to start spending."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1177233,
    "dDurationMs": 3233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All of that retirement money instead."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1180900,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if that happens,\nany other central bank would raise"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1184400,
    "dDurationMs": 3933,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "interest rates to slow down\nspending and thereby inflation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1188733,
    "dDurationMs": 5233,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But as we have just seen, that option\nwill be very costly for hedge fund Japan."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1194433,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So could it be that Japan's central bank\nwill have no choice"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1198600,
    "dDurationMs": 2766,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but just to let inflation increase"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1201366,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ever and ever more, making running Japan's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1204600,
    "dDurationMs": 3333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stable economy ever more difficult?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1209000,
    "dDurationMs": 1633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That could be true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1210633,
    "dDurationMs": 4033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in conclusion, Japan isn't bankrupt yet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1214666,
    "dDurationMs": 4034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because its net debt\nis actually much lower than we thought"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1218866,
    "dDurationMs": 3934,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because, well, they did go into debt\nto fund its aging population."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1222966,
    "dDurationMs": 3867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They got incredibly lucky\nwith their foreign investments."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1226833,
    "dDurationMs": 4367,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, this has locked hedge fund Japan\ninto a very tricky situation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1231200,
    "dDurationMs": 3166,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If it wants to keep\nits debt under control, not only does"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1234366,
    "dDurationMs": 4067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it need to control spending,\nit also needs to keep interest rates"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1238700,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "very low indeed,\nand it will need to keep the yen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1242300,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "relatively weak to prevent its assets\nfrom reducing in value too much."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1247633,
    "dDurationMs": 2867,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Can it actually pull this off\nas its population"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1250500,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "continues to age super rapidly?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1253700,
    "dDurationMs": 1333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We will just have to see."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1255033,
    "dDurationMs": 3967,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I actually think that our massive foreign\ninvestment position still makes sense,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1259300,
    "dDurationMs": 4333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "given that the rest of the world is simply\nstill much younger than Japan."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1263700,
    "dDurationMs": 3266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I have to admit,\nwe have never seen aging on this scale"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1266966,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before, so I do\nthink there is a genuine case to be made"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1270100,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that Japan will soon be known\nas the land of the rising inflation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1274600,
    "dDurationMs": 2066,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Indeed, the first signs are already here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1276666,
    "dDurationMs": 4934,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After decades of stable\nprices, prices are going up again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1281600,
    "dDurationMs": 566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In Japan."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1282166,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is already inflation back in Japan."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1285500,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is very worrying indeed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1287400,
    "dDurationMs": 2333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But yeah, that is my take.\nWhat do you think?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1289733,
    "dDurationMs": 1767,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let me know in the comments below."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1291500,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you want to make videos like I do,\ndefinitely go"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1294400,
    "dDurationMs": 4366,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "check out our sponsor Storyblocks\nin the description of this video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1298833,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "See you next time."
    } ]
  } ]
}
